## Web UI & admin/security rules (do not regress)

### Entry point & layering
- `publisher_v2.web.app` hosts the FastAPI app and routes; keep routes thin and delegate to existing services/orchestrator.
- The UI is a **single-page** template: `publisher_v2.web.templates.index.html` (vanilla JS + CSS, no build toolchain).

### Admin visibility & protections
- Admin-only controls (analyze, publish, status/admin panels) must **not be visible** to non-admin users; hide entirely rather than disable.
- Admin mode requires **both**:
  - HTTP auth (`WEB_AUTH_TOKEN` Bearer or `WEB_AUTH_USER`/`WEB_AUTH_PASS` Basic), and
  - an active admin cookie managed by `publisher_v2.web.auth` (e.g., `pv2_admin`).
- Admin cookie TTL is enforced server-side via `WEB_ADMIN_COOKIE_TTL_SECONDS` (clamped 60–3600s).
- The server is the source of truth: `/api/admin/status` and 401/403 must clear admin state client-side.

### Responsiveness & UX
- Mobile-first: no horizontal scrolling for core actions on common smartphone widths (~320–768px).
- Preserve the admin dark-red theme and keep contrast accessible where feasible.

### Contracts
- Preserve documented endpoint contracts in `docs_v2/03_Architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` and `docs_v2/roadmap/`.
